commit db7b9810562482054cc9d3afbc8ba8d8071df0cc

C03: the consent to read a confirmed capture is keyed by the capture, not by a mission id (SCREEN1407)

SCREEN1405 measured the reviewed screen reading on the mission-bound consent: the capture was approved, completed and verified, and ocr.read still asked a second confirmation. Each plan step carries its own mission id by construction (PreparedOperation.Create issues a fresh one per operation), so a consent bound to the capture's mission id can never match the read that follows it.

MissionEngine: a capture completed and verified under a granted confirmation records its captureId with a ten-minute consent window; an ocr.read or vision.describe over that captureId within the window is allowed without a new challenge, whatever its mission id; expired entries are dropped. The capture id is unguessable and exists only because the person confirmed that capture.

Kernel recompiled (BUILD1407). Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


